// Immerse's server for v2 (Backend/SETUP.md). Every value is empty here, so a build made from the repository alone,
// and every v1 build, has no server: it shows nothing of Group Films, never starts Clerk and never reaches a network
// service. A Mac that builds against the real or a local server copies Server.local.xcconfig.example to
// Server.local.xcconfig (ignored by git) and fills it in.
IMMERSE_CONVEX_URL =
IMMERSE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY =
// The host of a Group Film's link, https://<host>/j/<code>, and the support address reports go to (v2 Stage 2). Empty
// here, so a build from the repository alone has neither.
IMMERSE_JOIN_HOST =
IMMERSE_SUPPORT_ADDRESS =
// The entitlements a v2 build needs: Sign in with Apple, push and Declared Age Range. Empty here, so a v1 build signs
// with none of them and needs no change to the App ID.
IMMERSE_V2_ENTITLEMENTS =
// The mini-app (v2 Stage 3). The App Group is the container the full app and the App Clip keep Group Films in, so a
// mini-app guest's place, Roll and pictures are there when the full app is installed. The two entitlements files are
// the App Clip's own and the full app's when the App Clip is embedded in it (the ImmerseWithClip scheme). All empty
// here: a build from the repository alone has no App Group, signs with no entitlements, and its App Clip can open no
// event.
IMMERSE_APP_GROUP =
IMMERSE_CLIP_ENTITLEMENTS =
IMMERSE_V2_WITH_CLIP_ENTITLEMENTS =
#include? "Server.local.xcconfig"
